message: "If you use GraphSplit in your research, please cite the software using this metadata."
title: "GraphSplit: Sparse graph relocation from synchronized differential travel times"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Heimisson"
    given-names: "Elías Rafn"
    affiliation: "Institute of Earth Sciences, University of Iceland"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8342-7226"
repository-code: "https://github.com/eliasrh/GraphSplit"
url: "https://github.com/eliasrh/GraphSplit"
license: "LicenseRef-GraphSplit-NonCommercial-1.0"
version: "0.1.3"
date-released: "2026-08-13"
keywords:
  - seismology
  - earthquake relocation
  - double difference
  - graph methods
  - differential travel times
  - eikonal equation
abstract: >
  GraphSplit is a standard-library-only Julia implementation of sparse,
  graph-based earthquake relocation from synchronized DDSync theta data. It
  includes native Cartesian and radial layered-model travel-time builders,
  robust matrix-free inversion, serial-ID-safe input handling, and TOML-driven
  reproducible runs.
